48:## Prepared native Unison service
50:`railway.ts` keeps the undeployed `unison` service and `unison-data` volume out of the default resource graph. Set `NOTORGANIC_PREPARE_UNISON_SERVICE=1` only for a separately reviewed native-service plan. Once provisioned, keep the corresponding flag set for subsequent whole-project reconciliations; omitting a managed resource can propose deletion. The standalone docs service is likewise excluded unless `NOTORGANIC_PREPARE_DOCS_SERVICE=1`; production docs and identity domains currently terminate on landing. It does not change gateway/portal backend selection. The native service uses one replica and mounts `/data`; application commits reach SQLite through the compiled runtime's storage interpreter. A volume on the stock in-memory Cloud interpreter would not supply durability.
54:Local image proof is `rtk proxy python3 unison/container-smoke.py`, after the direct compiled-service proof has stopped. It uses synthetic credentials and a disposable local certificate, checks Docker health and verified HTTPS, then kills/restarts the non-root container on its fixture volume. It never pushes an image or contacts Railway.
56:A git-only Railway build lacks the ignored prebuilt artifact. Supply the isolated artifact context described in the runbook to the verified native service after separate deployment authorization, or prepare a reviewed CI artifact stage. Never upload the whole `.local` directory; it can contain state, logs and fixture keys. Remote context acceptance is still unproven.
58:The image is non-root (`10001:10001`), requires a writable mount owned by that identity, and healthchecks the compiled service over loopback. The external/private listener is HTTPS-only on port 8443; compiled HTTP binds to 127.0.0.1:8765. No public domain is declared. Pilot origin is `https://unison.railway.internal:8443/s/notorganic`. Supply PEM TLS secrets with a matching DNS SAN and configure the operator-managed CA in actual pilot clients; never disable verification. Railway's HTTP readiness probe is left unset for this TLS-only service; startup/Docker readiness and a private HTTPS check must pass before pilot traffic.
60:Required preserved secrets: `NOTORGANIC_INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY` (at least 32 characters), `NOTORGANIC_ADMIN_DIDS` (exact comma-separated DIDs), `NOTORGANIC_TLS_CERT`, `NOTORGANIC_TLS_KEY`. `preserve()` retains existing secrets but cannot populate an empty service. Database/environment names must remain stable; set `NOTORGANIC_UNISON_INITIALIZE=fresh-v2` once only after certifying an absent database, remove it after initialization and verify restart on the same volume.
62:The complete environment, ordering, backup/restore, upgrade and financial rollback procedure is [NATIVE-INTEGRATION.md, Proof and deployment](../unison/NATIVE-INTEGRATION.md#proof-and-deployment); storage limits are in [LIBRARIES.md](../unison/LIBRARIES.md#native-durable-backend-decision-2026-10-10), local results in [VERIFICATION.md](../unison/VERIFICATION.md#native-durability-round-4-2026-10-10). Follow [MONEY-CUTOVER.md](../unison/MONEY-CUTOVER.md) separately before any payment authority change. Production stays on Convex. Nothing in this preparation authorizes applying the IaC, creating resources, pushing an image or deploying.
66:The release integration preserves the live gateway volume by its existing name `gateway-volume` (50,000 MB, mounted at `/data/notorganic-evolution-artifacts`), landing domain routing, checkout configuration, OpenBao auto-unseal, portal waitlist settings, and PDS email/blob/backup settings. Live model prices, aliases, CORS origins, and product catalog entries use `preserve()` so applying an older source default cannot overwrite operational fixes. No secret values were exported.
